    "chunk_text": "(iv) Each Grama Niladhari\u2019sA copy of the electoral register in force containing all Polling District lyingOfficewithin the relevant Grama Niladhari\u2019s Division and copies of the related\u201cA\u201d and \u201cB\u201d Lists.\n\nI fldgi ( ^I& fPoh - YS% ,xld m%cd;dka;s%l iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha w;s \u00fafYI .ei\u00dc m;%h - 2019'08'23PART I : SEC. (I) - GAZETTE EXTRAORDINARY OF THE DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA - 23.08.201930A\n\n3. Any person whose name appears in the Register of Electors or the List \u201cB\u201d for the above Electoral District mayobject to the inclusion in such register of his/her own name or the name of any other person appearing in suchregister or List \u201cB\u201d or to the insertion or retention in the register of the name of any claimant, in duplicate to theRegistering Officer, Elections Office, Kegalle substantially in Form \u201cC\u201d or \u201cD\u201d as the case may be specified inthe Schedule to the said Act. Every objection to the inclusion of any name in the register should reach theRegistering Officer, Elections Office, Kegalle within four weeks from the date of publication of this notice inthe Gazette of the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka. Every objection in the insertion or retention ofthe register in the name of claimant should reach the Registering Officer within 14 days from the date on whicha notice containing the names of claimants is exhibited at the Elections Office, Kegalle.\n\nThis notice will be exhibited at the Elections Office, Kegalle from 23rd August 2019 to 19th September 2019.\n\n4. Forms for the purpose of making any claim or objection may be obtained from the above Elections Office,Divisional Secretariat, each Grama Niladhari\u2019s Office and each Local Authority in the Administrative District ofKegalle.\n\nS. W. WELGAMA,Assistant Registering Officer,Electoral District - No. : 22- Kegalle.District Elections Office,Kegalle,23rd August, 2019.\n\n09 -208/22\n\nPRINTED AT THE DEPARTMENT OF GOVERNMENT PRINTING, SRI LANKA."
