    "chunk_text": "5th AMENDMENT\n\nService Minute of the Sri Lanka Architects Service\n\nTHE Service Minute of the Sri Lanka Architects Service published in the Gazette Extraordinary No. 1877/28 dated 28th ofAugust, 2014 of the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka as amended by the Gazette Extraordinary No. 1882/18 dated01st of October 2014, No. 1952/20 dated 02nd of February 2016, No.1994/68 dated 24th of November 2016 and No. 2085/46dated 24th of August 2018 of the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka is amended as follows and these amendedprovisions will be made effective from 26th of February 2019, the date on which the Cabinet of Ministers made the policydecision.\n\nBy order of the Public Service Commission,\n\nM. A. B. DAYA SENARATH,Secretary,Public Service Commission.\n\n07th August, 2019.\n\nw;s \u00fafYI\n\nwxl 2137$88 - 2019 wf.daia;= ui 23 jeks isl=rdod - 2019'08'23No. 2137/88 - FRIDAY, AUGUST 23, 2019\n\nEXTRAORDINARYThe Gazette of the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka\n\n(Published by Authority)PART I : SECTION (I) \u2014 GENERAL\n\nGovernment Notifications\n\nY%S ,xld m%cd;dka;%sl iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha .ei\u00dc m;%h\n\n1A - G 30817 - 17 (08/2019)This Gazette Extraordinary can be downloaded from www. documents.gov.lk\n\n2 AI fldgi: (I) fPoh - Y%S ,xld m%cd;dka;%sl iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha w;s \u00fafYI .ei\u00dc m;%h - 2019'08'23PART 1: SEC. (1) - GAZETTE EXTRAORDINARY OF THE DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA - 23.08.2019\n\n10.1.1.1\n\n(II) Should have completed at least six (06) years of active and satisfactory period of service in Grade III of thecategory of service and earned six (06) salary increments.\n\n(III)Should have demonstrated a performance at satisfactory level or above during six (06) years immediately precedingthe date of promotion in accordance with the approved procedure of performance appraisal.\n\n10.2.1\n\n(I)Should have completed at least six (06) years of active and satisfactory period of service in Grade II of thecategory of service and earned six (06) salary increments."
