    "chunk_text": "(1) (a) in respect of a road declared by the Minister of Road as a provincial road, thelimit of constructing buildings in accordance with the distance decided by theProvincial Road Director, towards both sides from the the road center line ofthat road and the weight limit of the vehicle with total weight loaded, includingmaterials, people and animals should be published in the Gazette by theProvincial Road Director.\n\n2. Subsection 26(4) of the main Statute is replaced with the following new subsection and, itshall come into operation as subsection 26(4) of the main Statute.\n\n(4) The limits ordered by the above subsection (1) can be amended by the ProvincialRoad Director after having considered the recommendation received by a committeeappointed by the Provincial Road Director including two chief engineers of the UvaProvincial Department of Road Development and, the aforesaid amendment can beamended by an announcement published in the Gazette.\n\nUVA PROVINCIAL COUNCIL\n\nStatute (Amendment) of Uva Provincial Road of No. .......... of 2019 of the Uva Provincial Council\n\nA Statute came into operation for amending the Statute of \u201cUva Provincial Road\u201d of No. 02 of 2010 of the Uva ProvincialCouncil.\n\nBe it enacted as such by the Uva Province Provincial Council of the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lankain accordance with the powers vested to provincial councils through the 13th Amendment to the Constitution of theDemocratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka.\n\nShort title and dateof operation\n\nAmendment of theSection 3 of themain Statute\n\nAmendment ofSection 26 of themain Statute\n\nBuildingconstructionlimits and weightlimsits\n\n3AIV (w) jeks fldgi \u2014 Y%S ,xld m%cd;dka;s%l iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha w;s \u00fafYI .ei\u00dc m;%h - 2019'08'30PART IV(A) \u2014 GAZETTE EXTRAORDINARY OF THE DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA - 30.08.2019\n\n3. Subsection 26(6) of the main Statute is replaced by following new Subsection and, it shallcome into operation as subsection 26(6) of the main Statute."
