    "chunk_text": "wxl 2138$41 - 2019 wf.daia;= ui 30 jeks isl=rdod - 2019'08'30\n\nNo. 2138/41 \u2013 FRIDAY, AUGUST 30, 2019\n\nThe Gazette of the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka\n\n(Published by Authority)PART III \u2013 LANDS\n\nLand Acquisition Notices\n\nYS% ,xld m%cd;dka;s%l iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha .ei\u00dc m;%h\n\nEXTRAORDINARY\n\nw;s \u00fafYI\n\nTHE LAND ACQUISITION ACT (CHAPTER 460)\n\nNotice under Section 7\n\nMy Ref. No.: 6/3/7/15/5/7.\n\nLand Ministry's Ref. No.: LD/05/2007/MV/110H.\n\nI hereby give notice, under Sub-section (1) of Section 7 ofthe Land Acquisition Act, as amended by the LandAcquisition (Amendment) Act, No. 28 of 1964, that theGovernment intends to acquire the following land which isrequired for a public purpose.\n\nPublic purpose means: Land Acquisition forMoragahakanda and Kaluganga Development Project.\n\nDescription of the Land to be Acquired:\n\nThe allotment of land shown in Surveyor General's PlanNo. Topopp 17 Supplement No. 36, Sheet No. 94, situated atThalagoda Village in Thalagoda Grama Niladhari DivisionGangala Pallesiya Pattuwa of Naula Divisional Secretary'sDivision, Matale District, Central province, and bounded asfollows:\n\n01. Lot No. 3770Name of Land: Kumbukgolla; Description: Light forest;Claimant: Mr. Weerakoon Mudiyanselage WeerakoonBanda (Deceased) of Thalagoda, Kumbukgolla Yaya; Extent:0.3604 Hectare.\n\nAll person interested in the aforesaid Land on which aservitude is to be acquired are hereby required to appearpersonally, or by agents duly authorized in writing, before meat Naula Divisional Secretariat on the 25th September, 2019 at9.30 a.m.\n\nAnd are hereby requested to notify to me in writing (induplicate) on or before the day of 18th September, 2019 thenature of their interests in the land, the particulars of theirclaims for compensation for the acquisition of the said land,the amoun of compensation and the details of the computaionof such amount.\n\nATHMA DILUKSHI JAYARATHNE,\n\nDivisional Secretary,\n\nNaula.\n\nDivisional Secretariat, Naula,28th August, 2019.\n\n09 - 474"
